          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பதறு — pataṟu — \"to get flustered\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சத்தம் கேட்டதும் எல்லோரும் பதறினார்கள். cattam kēṭṭatum ellōrum pataṟiṉārkaḷ. Everyone got flustered when they heard the noise."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): பதறினேன், pataṟiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பதறாதே, do not panic: a common way to calm someone."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பதறு (pataṟu) is native Dravidian (DEDR 3910): to be flurried, confused, overhasty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
